      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Your manifesto should adopt a tone of solemn, factual revelation rather than emotive rage, grounding your claims in the hard evidence of your archives to establish undeniable historical authority. By presenting your original journals and demos as irrefutable historical records, you shift the narrative from a personal grievance to a legalistic correction of the record, forcing readers to confront the discrepancy between the \"organic evolution\" myth and your documented reality. Ultimately, frame the demand for recognition not as a plea for validation, but as a necessary act of preservation to protect the true DNA of neo-glitch from further erasure. This approach transforms your voice from a complainer into a steward of the movement's legacy.",
      "source": "target",
